:null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Azenta, Inc. provides biological and chemical compound sample exploration and management solutions for the life sciences industry in the United States, China, the United Kingdom, rest of Europe, the Asia Pacific, and internationally. It operates through Sample Management Solutions and Multiomics segments. The Sample Management Solutions segment provides sample management products and services, including automated stores, cryogenic systems, automated sample tubes, consumables and instruments, and controlled rate thawing devices, as well as sample repository services. This segment also offers consultation services to clients throughout their experimental design and implementation processes. The Multiomics segment provides genomic and other sample analysis services comprising gene sequencing, gene synthesis, and related services. The company was formerly known as Brooks Automation, Inc. and changed its name to Azenta, Inc. in December 2021. Azenta, Inc. was founded in 1978 and is headquartered in Burlington, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Martin D. Madaus D.V.M., Ph.D. | Interim President, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $83,750 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $218K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Azenta, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.0B market cap on $622M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -2.6pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at -2% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $27M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -5.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 151% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5119215404058879},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (19.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.6pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 28% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here\u2019s What Boosted Investor Confidence in Azenta (AZTA)","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/boosted-investor-confidence-azenta-azta-154333197.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795707813.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.936,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(AZTA) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/40/AZTA_Price_Dynamics_and_Execution-Aware_Positioning_112026120201_1795150921.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795150921.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Azenta (NASDAQ:AZTA) Upgraded at Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/17/azenta-nasdaqazta-upgraded-at-wall-street-zen.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794912826.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"How Did Azenta (NASDAQ:AZTA) Grow Revenue and What Is Its New Outlook?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/smallcap/how-did-azenta-nasdaqazta-grow-revenue-and-what-is-its-new-out